e connection. Writing body data first still returns `errHijackAlreadyWritten`.\n\nI added a test case \"hijack after header write should succeed\" to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`. The gate check passed: the test fails without the fix and passes with it.\n\nI didn't run the full test suite or try it with a real websocket library.","ttft_ms":4641,"type":"result","duration_ms":21018,"uuid":"337b6df6-f643-42d0-a527-48db6a94bea3","ttft_stream_ms":846,"time_to_request_ms":138,"first_content_frame_ms":846,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
